+# Release notes and versions
+
+## Recommended convention — October 21, 2026
+
+Use **vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH** for site releases and a short descriptive GitHub Release title. Major marks a redesign/platform era; minor marks a named feature milestone; patch marks a focused fix or small improvement within the current milestone. This is a website release convention, not a package API compatibility promise. This recommendation awaits John's release review; it does not create a tag.
+
+| Item | Convention / recommendation |
+| --- | --- |
+| Browser exclusion #66 | **v2.0.1 — Cleaner analytics**, proposed next available patch |
+| Mentoring #54 | **v2.1.0 — Mentoring**, preserving its reservation |
+| Optional staging candidate | `v2.0.1-rc.1`, then `-rc.2` when useful |
+| Feature branch | `feat/66-exclude-own-traffic` from current `main` |
+| Fix / cleanup branches | `fix/<issue>-<short-name>` / `chore/<short-name>` |
+| Version source | Annotated Git release tag at the verified production commit; npm command manifest stays unversioned |
+
+Only the historical **Ver1** tag/release existed at inspection. Preserve it. October 2 V2 launch and October 14 initial dashboard are documented unversioned deliveries; do not invent old tags or dates.
+
+## Release notes workflow
+
+Maintain [CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/johnapaz/johnapaz.github.io/blob/feat/66-exclude-own-traffic/CHANGELOG.md) in source. Add user-visible entries under Unreleased during feature work. At release, move only the shipped entries to the selected version/date and publish matching GitHub Release notes with the actual production SHA, previous SHA, validation/deployment evidence, limitations and rollback. Never move a published tag.
+
+CI build success, staging review, Pages deployment and the protected Cloudflare Worker are separate evidence. For #66, public Admin and the control page ship via Pages; the private dashboard shortcut needs a reconciled Worker asset deployment. If the shortcut is deferred, disclose that and keep its work open. No final tag or release is published by draft PR #67.
+
+## Current draft — Cleaner analytics
+
+Exclude this browser / Undo stops future collection while preserving consent. Available through the existing consent panel and an always-untracked preferences page. Mark each browser/device and production/staging separately. Clearing storage/private browsing can remove the setting. Earlier visits remain in reports; no owner identity or historical report filter is introduced.
+
+See [PR #67](https://github.com/johnapaz/johnapaz.github.io/pull/67), [#66](https://github.com/johnapaz/johnapaz.github.io/issues/66), and the [release guide](https://github.com/johnapaz/johnapaz.github.io/blob/feat/66-exclude-own-traffic/docs/releasing.md). Local analytics/exclusion regressions and all six protected backend tests passed. CI, staging UI/network, keyboard/narrow/device verification and release coordination remain to be recorded.
